                                'An orienteering map is a precise, detailed representation of the terrain. Special colours and symbols show roads, paths, buildings, fences, water features, rocks, vegetation and landforms. Map scale helps judge real distance, and north lines help orient the map correctly. Fast, accurate map reading is one of the core skills of orienteering.'
